    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0118" n="1236" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p2/pg1236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Matthews
                    files, lot 53 D 413: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of Staff, United States Army (Collins) to the Commander in
                        Chief Far East (Clark)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>operational immediate</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-06-22T18:34:00-04:00">June 22, 1953—6:34
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>DA 942047. From CSUSA for CINCUNC. This is a
                    joint State–Defense message. Reur message DTG 221100Z from Hq ArmyEight.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d625-f1"/></p>
                <p>Believe that you should make no commitment to Rhee at your next meeting on suggestions for changes in POW agreement contained in para 5<hi
                        rendition="#italic">d</hi> of reference message but listen to what he has to
                    say. In general believe Rhee should not be
                    encouraged to think we are prepared to renegotiate armistice agreement. However,
                    we are interested in Rhee’s reaction to
                    your suggestion. Suggest you submit summary of Rhee’s reaction and follow up with such additional comments as
                    result from discussion of this and other aspects of situation with Robertson and Collins.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
